  "worked_solution": "A function $h(x)$ is concave down over an interval $(a,b)$ if ${h}^{\u2033}(x)<0$ for all $x\\in (a,b).$\n\nOn the given graph of $y={h}^{\u2033}(x),$ we can see that ${h}^{\u2033}(x)<0$ on the intervals $(-4,-2)$ and $(2,4).$  Therefore, the function $h(x)$ is concave down on the intervals $(-4,-2)$ and $(2,4).$",
